# An allow list rather than a deny list: exclude everything, then name the
# handful of paths the Dockerfile actually COPYs. A deny list would have to be
# extended every time something new turns up in the working directory, and the
# cost of forgetting is silent — a live database or an editor's state directory
# gets shipped to the daemon as part of the build context. Here the cost of
# forgetting is a COPY that fails loudly on the next push, since CI builds the
# image every time.
#
# The build context currently in the working directory but deliberately kept
# out includes data/ (the running instance's SQLite database, its WAL and its
# shared memory file), ignored/, the built ./mylinks binary, .git, and the
# .idea/.claude/.junie editor and tool directories.
#
# Keep in step with the COPY lines in the Dockerfile.
#
# One trap when editing: these patterns are anchored to the context root and are
# not recursive, unlike .gitignore. `!ui` re-includes the ui directory at the
# root and everything under it, but it does not mean "any directory named ui at
# any depth".
*

# Builder stage: dependencies, then the source. ui/ is not copied here, it is
# replaced by empty-efs.go and empty/ so the binary reads its assets from disk
# instead of embedding them.
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!empty-efs.go
!empty

# Final stage: the launcher and the real assets, served from disk at runtime.
!run.sh
!ui
